### 🚀 Feature Proposal

Under the [OpenAPI 3.0 specifications](https://swagger.io/docs/specification/describing-responses/), "Empty Response Body" explains that responses such as 204 No Content can omit the `content` and just have a description. This should be an allowed feature.

### Motivation

This is useful as it covers the full specification.

### Example

I have tried to do this...
```js
{
    schema: {
        ...
        response: {
            204: {
                description: "Session deleted"
            }
        }
    }
}
```
...but it currently errors
```
FastifyError [Error]: Failed building the serialization schema for DELETE: /users/sessions/@me, due to error schema is invalid: data/properties/description must be object,boolean
```
I have to include a `type: "object"` and empty `properties: {}` for it to build. Having only a description should be supported.

